    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance, tgs:PracticeCluster.SystemicFinance ;
    dcterms:description "The Osa Biocultural Fund is a flexible tool to seed community-run work in food sovereignty, ecological The Osa Biocultural Fund is a flexible tool to seed community-run work in food sovereignty, ecological restoration, arts, and education."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.OsaRegenerativeLearningCenterElLocal a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Osa Regenerative Learning Center (El Local)"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ReGenerOsaCollective ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.CulturalHubOrLearningCenter, tgs:PracticeTerm.TraditionalEcologicalKnowledge ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.HubsAndCenters, tgs:PracticeCluster.WaysOfKnowing ;
    dcterms:description "El Local is a community hub and learning center that anchors regenerative projects. It hosts youth programs, intergenerational exchange, local storytelling, and skills for land-based living."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.ReGenerOsaWomensGovernanceCircle a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "ReGenerOsa Women's Governance Circle"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ReGenerOsaCollective ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.GovernanceBodies ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance ;
    dcterms:description "ReGenerOsa is guided by what it calls the Council of Eight—a circle of eight long-serving local women leaders, including Indigenous, campesina, and Afro–Costa Rican elders—who set direction and keep activities accountable to place-based wisdom."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.StoneSoupSocial a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stone Soup Social"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ReGenerOsaCollective ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.CongressingAndEvents, tgs:PracticeTerm.NetworkWeaving ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance ;
    dcterms:description "Like many efforts here, it began with food. The first gathering was a stone soup social—people brought ingredients, shared a meal, and started to meet."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.BeudaDemocraticInnovationProject a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Beuda Democratic Innovation Project"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ResilienceEarth ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.GovernanceBodies, tgs:PracticeTerm.ParticipatoryStrategies ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance ;
    dcterms:description "They began seven years ago in Beuda, one of the smallest towns in La Garrotxa. Oscar says starting from the edge made sense: “It would be really difficult for us to start in the center because you know ruralities can be quite resistant to change behaviors sometimes.” Several municipalities were shifting away from…"@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.DemocracyFestivalFestivalIltir a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Democracy Festival (Festival Iltir)"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ResilienceEarth ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.CongressingAndEvents, tgs:PracticeTerm.NetworkWeaving ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance ;
    dcterms:description "To channel energy around that tension, they launched a Democracy Festival (Festival Iltir)—a space to surface what was moving."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.LaGarrotxa2030StrategicPlanningInitiative a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "La Garrotxa 2030 Strategic Planning Initiative"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ResilienceEarth ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.NetworkWeaving, tgs:PracticeTerm.ParticipatoryStrategies, tgs:PracticeTerm.SocioeconomicIndicators ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance, tgs:PracticeCluster.MappingAndIndicators ;
    dcterms:description "In late 2019, participatory governance was spreading across La Garrotxa; several rural municipalities had piloted citizen participation, often co-designed and facilitated by Resilience Earth."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.LocalGovernmentIncubatorINCAT a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Local Government Incubator (INCAT)"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ResilienceEarth ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.GovernanceBodies, tgs:PracticeTerm.LearningPrograms ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.CommunityGovernance, tgs:PracticeCluster.WaysOfKnowing ;
    dcterms:description "Last year they opened an incubator for local governments—after many incubators for co-ops and nonprofits."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.ArtsAndMuseumOfTheFuture a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    skos:prefLabel "Arts & Museum of the Future"@en ;
    thinkr:carriedOutBy tgs:Organization.ReVillageGreenValley ;
    thinkr:hasPracticeTerm tgs:PracticeTerm.ArtAndStorytelling ;
    thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster tgs:PracticeCluster.WaysOfKnowing ;
    dcterms:description "On site they developed a “Museum of the Future”: archives and time capsules honor seven generations back; school visits and participatory visioning imagine seven generations forward—a place where past and future meet in the present and stories of land and people can be held while new possibilities are shaped together."@en ;
    dcterms:source tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology ;
    .

tgs:Initiative.CommunityLandTrustFormation a thinkr:Initiative, owl:NamedIndividual ;
